.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt LIBSODIUM-ADA 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libsodium-ada
.Nd Ada 2022 binding to the libsodium cryptographic library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
with Crypto;
with Crypto.Sign;
with Crypto.Box;
.Ed
.Pp
The library is linked with
.Fl lcrypto_ada
and
.Fl lsodium ,
and is selected in a GNAT project file with
.Ql with "crypto";
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a thin, complete Ada 2022 binding to
.Xr libsodium 3 .
It maps each libsodium primitive onto an idiomatic Ada package: fixed-size
buffers are
.Vt Crypto.Byte_Array
slices, error returns become exceptions
.Pq Vt Crypto.Crypto_Error ,
and opaque C state is hidden behind private types.
No raw pointers escape the binding.
.Pp
The root package
.Vt Crypto
holds the core utilities and primitives; the higher-level suites are child
packages
.Vt Crypto.Sign ,
.Vt Crypto.Box ,
and so on.
Call
.Fn Crypto.Init
once before use (it is idempotent).
.Sh CORE PACKAGE
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Vt Crypto
Library initialisation and version, random bytes
.Pq Fn Random , Fn Random_Uniform , Fn Random_Deterministic ,
SHA-256/SHA-512
.Pq Fn Hash_Sha256 , Fn Hash_Sha512 ,
HMAC
.Pq Fn Hmac_Sha256 , Fn Hmac_Sha512 ,
base-64 and hex encoding, constant-time comparison
.Pq Fn Verify_16 , Fn Verify_32 , Fn Verify_64 , Fn Constant_Time_Equal ,
little-endian big-number helpers
.Pq Fn Increment , Fn Add ,
deterministic wipe
.Pq Fn Memzero ,
ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD
.Pq Fn Seal , Fn Open ,
deterministic padding
.Pq Fn Pad , Fn Unpad ,
CPU feature detection
.Pq Fn Runtime_Has_* ,
and a misuse handler
.Pq Fn Set_Misuse_Handler .
The guarded
.Vt Secure_Buffer
type wraps
.Fn sodium_malloc / sodium_free
storage with
.Fn Mlock , Fn Munlock , Fn Protect , Fn Wipe , Fn Fill , and Fn Contents .
.El
.Sh CHILD PACKAGES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Vt Crypto.Sign
Ed25519 signatures: key generation, detached and attached signing,
verification, key conversion, and a streaming (pre-hashed) form.
.It Vt Crypto.Box
Public-key authenticated encryption (Curve25519-XSalsa20-Poly1305), combined
and detached modes, a precomputed shared key, and anonymous sealed boxes.
.It Vt Crypto.Scalarmult
Scalar multiplication over Curve25519 and Ristretto255.
.It Vt Crypto.Kx
X25519 key exchange, deriving per-side session-key pairs.
.It Vt Crypto.Secretbox
Symmetric authenticated encryption (XSalsa20-Poly1305).
.It Vt Crypto.Secretstream
Encrypted streams (XChaCha20-Poly1305) with per-message tags.
.It Vt Crypto.Generichash
BLAKE2b, keyed or unkeyed, one-shot or streaming.
.It Vt Crypto.Shorthash
SipHash-2-4, a short keyed hash.
.It Vt Crypto.Auth
HMAC-SHA512-256 message authentication.
.It Vt Crypto.Onetimeauth
Poly1305 one-time authentication.
.It Vt Crypto.Pwhash
Password hashing: Argon2id/Argon2i and scrypt, raw and encoded-string forms.
.It Vt Crypto.Stream
Stream ciphers (XSalsa20, XChaCha20, ChaCha20, Salsa20), keystream and XOR.
.It Vt Crypto.Aead
The four AEAD primitives (ChaCha20-Poly1305 IETF/non-IETF, XChaCha20-Poly1305,
AES-256-GCM) under a single variant type.
.El
.Sh CONVENTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Byte_Array
All keys, nonces, digests and messages are
.Vt Crypto.Byte_Array ,
an unconstrained array of stream elements indexed from 1.
.It Sizes
Each primitive exposes named size constants
.Pq e.g. Vt Crypto.Sign.Signature_Size .
Subprograms raise
.Vt Crypto.Crypto_Error
when a buffer is not the required length.
.It Errors
Authentication and decryption failures raise
.Vt Crypto.Crypto_Error
rather than returning a boolean, except the
.Fn Verify
predicates, which return
.Dv False .
.It Secure_Buffer
A single-owner handle to guarded, page-aligned memory; do not copy it.
.It State
Streaming state types
.Pq Vt Crypto.State_Buffer
are passed back to the library by reference and must not be copied between
matching
.Fn Update
calls.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sodium 7
.Pp
The authoritative API reference is the package specifications themselves,
installed with the library
.Po
.Vt Crypto ,
.Vt Crypto.Sign ,
.Vt Crypto.Box ,
\&...
.Pc .
Full documentation of the underlying library is at
.Lk https://doc.libsodium.org/ .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An David Walther
